messages:
meera: FYI I opened a docs PR that updates the Console observability snippets and the dashboard JSON for the metrics-v3 migration. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/512 — main changes are metric renames and a new tracing hook example. PTAL when you have a minute.

alex: Nice. What's the user-visible change? Anything that will break existing dashboards?

meera: The biggest change is name normalization: cost_bytes -> cost_usd and latency_ms stays but we now add label 'route' for per-route breakdown. Also the tracing hook API in the snippet changed to: `console.observability.attachTrace(req, { route: 'api.generate' })`. The old snippet used a raw trace id field.

jon: Can you paste the new snippet inline? I'll try it against local staging.

meera: Sure — here's the JS example from the PR:

```js
// attach tracing and populate route label for dashboard grouping
import { observability } from 'redwood-console';

app.post('/generate', async (req, res) => {
  const trace = observability.attachTrace(req, { route: 'api.generate' });
  // ensure cost label is set on events we emit
  observability.emitCostEvent({ trace, cost_usd: estimateCost(req.body) });
  const out = await generate(req.body);
  res.json(out);
});
```

patrick: I also found a couple of 404s in the dashboard embed links in the old migration guide — left a comment in the PR. docs-bot just flagged one broken anchor.

docs-bot: link-checker: 1 broken link detected in README/migration.md -> /console/old-dashboard#cost-breakdown

meera: Thanks — fixed that anchor and updated the redirect target. Also added a migration note explaining that dashboards using `cost_bytes` will need the small rename to `cost_usd` and to multiply by the USD conversion factor if you were storing raw byte counts.

alex: Good call. Can you add an explicit example showing the multiplier? Last time people were confused about units (tokens vs bytes vs cents).

meera: Done — added a short table and a one-line example: `cost_usd = cost_bytes * 0.000012` (example conversion, see PR for exact values per model).

jon: Quick nit: in the snippet you used `observability.emitCostEvent` but the SDK method is `observability.recordCost`. I left a tiny inline suggestion.

meera: Nice catch — fixed.

patrick: CI link-check is green now. I left one comment about wording in the migration intro. Otherwise LGTM.

meera: Thanks. Plan is to merge after a quick smoke test on staging. Staging dashboard URL: https://staging.console.redwood.ai/dashboards/obs-metrics-v3 (credentials in 1Password).

deploy-bot: Deploy scheduled to staging: 2026-03-22T15:10:00Z — plan: docs static site rebuild + dashboard JSON sync.

alex: I'll run the smoke and check trace->dashboard mapping after deploy. If anything flaps we can revert the dashboard JSON and keep the snippets.

meera: Awesome, appreciate it. If anyone hits anything weird ping me here or add a follow-up PR. :thumbsup:
